Yoshito...you...

101
00:06:59,340 --> 00:07:01,000
Maho won't answer.

102
00:07:06,580 --> 00:07:09,890
Main stage, 8,900 people.

103
00:07:09,890 --> 00:07:13,860
Second Stage, 980 people.

104
00:07:13,860 --> 00:07:17,690
And Third Stage, 8,100 people...

105
00:07:17,690 --> 00:07:19,960
and growing steadily!

106
00:07:21,200 --> 00:07:23,200
It's unbelievable,

107
00:07:23,200 --> 00:07:27,200
but if this keeps up,
Stage 3 will turn it around and win.

108
00:07:27,200 --> 00:07:30,110
The main stage keeps
losing spectators...

109
00:07:30,110 --> 00:07:34,540
and I don't see
the crowd lessening.

110
00:07:34,540 --> 00:07:38,150
But we've got trouble on Stage 3.

111
00:07:38,150 --> 00:07:40,150
The crowd has grown tremendously,

112
00:07:40,150 --> 00:07:43,650
but BECK hasn't
come back for an encore.

113
00:07:43,650 --> 00:07:45,290
Huh? Why?!

114
00:07:45,290 --> 00:07:46,990
Well, I...

115
00:07:46,990 --> 00:07:51,160
Encore! BECK! BECK!

116
00:07:51,160 --> 00:07:55,650
-Come out!
-Give us an encore!

117
00:07:59,670 --> 00:08:02,170
-Encore! Encore!
-Hey, that's...

118
00:08:02,170 --> 00:08:03,600
-Encore! Encore!
-No way!

119
00:08:05,340 --> 00:08:06,930
It's the vocalist for BECK!

120
00:08:10,680 --> 00:08:14,620
-Hey, he's running away! Hey! Wait!
-Wait! Wait!

121
00:08:18,020 --> 00:08:19,190
Maho!

122
00:08:19,190 --> 00:08:20,690
Let's go!

123
00:08:20,690 --> 00:08:21,950
Maho!

124
00:08:23,530 --> 00:08:26,030
-Koyuki!
-Maho!

125
00:08:26,030 --> 00:08:27,860
No one can follow us!

126
00:08:27,860 --> 00:08:29,700
No!

127
00:08:29,700 --> 00:08:31,630
Koyuki, you're too fast!

128
00:08:36,640 --> 00:08:37,970
You were watching?

129
00:08:39,310 --> 00:08:40,980
Uh-huh.

130
00:08:40,980 --> 00:08:44,040
After all, Koyuki...

131
00:08:46,150 --> 00:08:47,440
Koyuki...

132
00:08:48,820 --> 00:08:50,490
Koyuki...

133
00:08:50,490 --> 00:08:54,990
That was an awesome performance.
Seriously, I was blown away.

134
00:08:54,990 --> 00:08:57,620
Koyuki...you're so cool.

135
00:09:07,670 --> 00:09:09,830
This is gonna be our final live.

136
00:09:10,410 --> 00:09:11,510
Are you sure?

137
00:09:11,510 --> 00:09:12,730
Yeah.

138
00:09:15,680 --> 00:09:20,050
The next day, many great
bands performed on stage.

139
00:09:35,030 --> 00:09:37,690
Hey, Koyuki...Hurry it up.

140
00:09:37,970 --> 00:09:38,830
Uh-huh.

141
00:09:39,970 --> 00:09:41,300
Where's Chiba-kun?

142
00:09:41,300 --> 00:09:42,830
He's going home by train.

143
00:09:43,940 --> 00:09:44,840
Oh...

144
00:09:44,840 --> 00:09:46,830
He said he wants to be alone.

145
00:09:48,140 --> 00:09:52,910
I heard that a band named
BECK was great yesterday.

146
00:09:52,910 --> 00:09:53,650
Oh yeah?

147
00:09:53,650 --> 00:09:55,640
I really, really wanted to see that.

148
00:09:57,320 --> 00:09:58,290
Koyuki!

149
00:09:58,290 --> 00:09:59,980
Oh, sorry!

150
00:10:02,160 --> 00:10:06,150
Tomorrow and the day after
and the day after that...Time will pass.

151
00:10:07,660 --> 00:10:10,830
Regardless of what happens to BECK.

152
00:10:13,840 --> 00:10:15,840
Saku, take a look at this.

153
00:10:15,840 --> 00:10:17,670
Wow! Awesome!

154
00:10:19,840 --> 00:10:23,350
A month and a half has passed
since that live performance.

155
00:10:23,350 --> 00:10:25,010
What am I doing?

156
00:10:28,680 --> 00:10:30,850
Yukio, telephone!

157
00:10:30,850 --> 00:10:32,190
Who is it?

158
00:10:32,190 --> 00:10:34,350
Some lady named Sato.

159
00:10:37,290 --> 00:10:39,790
O-Ouch!

160
00:10:39,790 --> 00:10:43,630
Koyuki-kun, do you have some
time tomorrow afternoon?

161
00:10:43,630 --> 00:10:45,130
Huh? Tomorrow?

162
00:10:45,130 --> 00:10:47,600
In front of the station
by that dog. At one p.m.

163
00:10:49,140 --> 00:10:52,470
BECK's live performance
has become a legend.

164
00:10:52,470 --> 00:10:53,480
Oh...

165
00:10:53,480 --> 00:10:55,600
-I saw the magazine.
-Lots of things are being said,

166
00:10:56,640 --> 00:11:00,150
but it's impossible to get a true count
from that huge mass of people.

167
00:11:00,150 --> 00:11:03,150
Why did you want to see me?

168
00:11:03,150 --> 00:11:05,350
There's someone
who wants to meet you.

169
00:11:06,620 --> 00:11:08,490
Who is it?

170
00:11:08,490 --> 00:11:10,250
You'll be shocked.

171
00:11:11,830 --> 00:11:13,160
Welcome, Yukio.

172
00:11:13,160 --> 00:11:15,830
Let me get straight
to the point today.

173
00:11:15,830 --> 00:11:19,060
I'd like to talk about your
solo debut in the United States.

174
00:11:19,330 --> 00:11:20,860
Uh...Is this...

175
00:11:21,170 --> 00:11:24,010
He's Mr. Leon Sykes.

176
00:11:24,010 --> 00:11:27,270
He wants you to make
a solo debut across America.

177
00:11:31,480 --> 00:11:35,020
Don't you mess with me baby.

178
00:11:35,020 --> 00:11:38,680
Everybody knows I'm here.

179
00:11:41,860 --> 00:11:47,690
All I've got to say, yeah,
got my mind made up.

180
00:11:56,870 --> 00:11:58,130
This is a great guitar.

181
00:11:59,710 --> 00:12:01,540
I'll let you think about it.

182
00:12:01,540 --> 00:12:03,550
Great, man!

183
00:12:03,550 --> 00:12:07,880
We'll meet over and over again
to talk about this project.

184
00:12:07,880 --> 00:12:11,320
We released five gold discs
from RJ Label last year.

185
00:12:12,720 --> 00:12:17,060
Wow! Malcolm and Fat Jimmy
and Danger Soul!

186
00:12:17,060 --> 00:12:20,400
They're all at the top
of the charts right now!

187
00:12:20,400 --> 00:12:24,400
I'm sorry.
I can't accept your proposal.

188
00:12:24,400 --> 00:12:26,570
I'm returning the guitar, too.

189
00:12:26,570 --> 00:12:27,240
What?!

190
00:12:27,240 --> 00:12:29,740
H-Hey Koyuki-kun!

191
00:12:29,740 --> 00:12:32,570
Ah...I'll call you back later!

192
00:12:32,570 --> 00:12:33,410
Koyuki-kun!

193
00:12:33,410 --> 00:12:35,340
Boss! You want me to get him?

194
00:12:36,580 --> 00:12:38,850
Hey, do you understand
what you're doing?!

195
00:12:38,850 --> 00:12:39,850
Huh? Understand what?

196
00:12:39,850 --> 00:12:42,850
Cripes! This is the chance of a lifetime!

197
00:12:42,850 --> 00:12:44,850
It's never going to
come around again!

198
00:12:44,850 --> 00:12:48,690
-I can't believe this!
-Things are so boring lately.

199
00:12:48,690 --> 00:12:51,850
No one would notice
if I were gone.

200
00:12:58,870 --> 00:13:01,130
Ryusuke-kun...

201
00:13:04,870 --> 00:13:07,880
What? Ryusuke Minami
has disappeared?

202
00:13:07,880 --> 00:13:09,240
Yeah, Boss.

203
00:13:10,380 --> 00:13:13,380
Find him. And take him out!

204
00:13:13,380 --> 00:13:14,880
Yeah.

205
00:13:14,880 --> 00:13:18,320
But I guess we gotta take care
of that kid from yesterday, too, huh?

206
00:13:19,390 --> 00:13:20,980
You want me to put him on his back?

207
00:13:22,060 --> 00:13:23,730
I've never heard that kind of music...

208
00:13:23,730 --> 00:13:26,560
Like "Don't You Mess with Me."

209
00:13:26,560 --> 00:13:28,320
W-What'd you say, Boss?

210
00:13:31,900 --> 00:13:34,740
I'll never be part of a band again!

211
00:13:34,740 --> 00:13:36,240
-Huh?! That's...
-Huh!?

212
00:13:36,240 --> 00:13:38,170
I'm gonna use this shop
to train myself and learn

213
00:13:38,170 --> 00:13:41,840
with the goal of opening
a chain of ramen shops!

214
00:13:41,840 --> 00:13:46,350
Taira says he wants
to try a new band, too.

215
00:13:46,350 --> 00:13:48,840
But this ramen is pretty bad.

216
00:13:50,350 --> 00:13:53,340
-You should find
another shop to train at.
-Shut up!

217
00:13:55,360 --> 00:13:59,860
Please join our group,
Typhoon Stones, as a guitarist!

218
00:13:59,860 --> 00:14:02,860
Sorry, but I must refuse.

219
00:14:02,860 --> 00:14:05,030
There's a month till
our live performance.

220
00:14:05,030 --> 00:14:07,370
So please think it over. Please!

221
00:14:07,370 --> 00:14:08,800
Really, think about it!

222
00:14:10,710 --> 00:14:12,640
Please say yes!

223
00:14:14,210 --> 00:14:16,970
Why won't you join them
to help them out?

224
00:14:18,150 --> 00:14:19,640
Hmm...

225
00:14:20,720 --> 00:14:24,550
Koyuki, I wanna talk to you.

226
00:14:24,550 --> 00:14:26,890
Huh? Saku...

227
00:14:26,890 --> 00:14:29,220
I'm used to it.

228
00:14:29,220 --> 00:14:32,230
I mean, grade school,
middle school, high school.

229
00:14:32,230 --> 00:14:35,060
This will be the fifth time.

230
00:14:35,060 --> 00:14:40,000
But this time is harder than the rest...
changing schools like this.

231
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:44,510
Saku!

232
00:14:44,510 --> 00:14:47,680
It's still two months away.

233
00:14:47,680 --> 00:14:50,180
But I wanted to let you know first.

234
00:14:50,180 --> 00:14:51,680
Saku...

235
00:14:51,680 --> 00:14:56,520
Oh yeah...I want to
tell you one more thing.

236
00:14:56,520 --> 00:14:58,020
What is it?

237
00:14:58,020 --> 00:15:01,690
It may be too soon
to bring this up...

238
00:15:01,690 --> 00:15:05,860
But I may quit music after this.

239
00:15:05,860 --> 00:15:07,030
But...

240
00:15:07,030 --> 00:15:13,030
But Koyuki...
You must never quit music!

241
00:15:13,030 --> 00:15:13,870
Saku...

242
00:15:13,870 --> 00:15:15,300
I want you to write more
songs like "Slip Out"...

243
00:15:15,300 --> 00:15:20,540
...that truly moved people's hearts.

244
00:15:20,540 --> 00:15:22,210
What're you saying?!

245
00:15:22,210 --> 00:15:25,750
Saku, you're the one
who mustn't quit music!

246
00:15:25,750 --> 00:15:28,550
I've learned so much...

247
00:15:28,550 --> 00:15:31,050
...from you...

248
00:15:31,050 --> 00:15:32,250
Koyuki...

249
00:16:12,860 --> 00:16:15,700
Hey Tanaka...You were on tonight!

250
00:16:15,700 --> 00:16:17,700
Next time again, 'kay?

251
00:16:17,700 --> 00:16:20,370
Yeah, I'm amazed.

252
00:16:20,370 --> 00:16:22,040
See ya!

253
00:16:22,040 --> 00:16:25,040
Huh? Aren't you coming
to the wrap party?

254
00:16:25,040 --> 00:16:26,310
I was gonna try to convince him...

255
00:16:26,310 --> 00:16:29,970
...to be a permanent member
of the Typhoon Stones.

256
00:16:31,380 --> 00:16:34,380
It's been a while,
so I was nervous.

257
00:16:34,380 --> 00:16:36,820
Yeah, you haven't played
since Grateful Sound.

258
00:16:36,820 --> 00:16:37,650
Yeah...

259
00:16:37,650 --> 00:16:40,490
I helped out with a band
a couple of times,

260
00:16:40,490 --> 00:16:42,650
but I got nervous, too.

261
00:16:44,330 --> 00:16:47,160
But...something's missing.

262
00:16:47,160 --> 00:16:49,320
Something's totally missing.

263
00:16:50,500 --> 00:16:52,830
'Cuz I really had a taste of it.

264
00:16:52,830 --> 00:16:56,670
That BECK was a really special band.

265
00:17:15,020 --> 00:17:16,020
Sorry to keep you waiting!

266
00:17:16,020 --> 00:17:18,690
It's your last day, Saku...

267
00:17:18,690 --> 00:17:20,360
So let's really party up!

268
00:17:20,360 --> 00:17:21,390
Yeah!

269
00:17:22,530 --> 00:17:24,130
Hey Saku, not bad!

270
00:17:24,630 --> 00:17:25,900
Wow!

271
00:17:25,900 --> 00:17:28,870
Hey Koyuki! Get a strike!

272
00:17:32,370 --> 00:17:34,540
-No way!
-Oh no!

273
00:17:34,540 --> 00:17:36,440
Yes! Six wins in a row!

274
00:17:36,440 --> 00:17:37,480
Yay!

275
00:17:37,480 --> 00:17:39,650
Hey, let's change teams.

276
00:17:39,650 --> 00:17:41,650
I want to be with Saku!

277
00:17:41,650 --> 00:17:44,720
Darn it! One more game!

278
00:17:44,720 --> 00:17:46,310
Huh?!

279
00:17:51,430 --> 00:17:53,660
Isn't their ramen great?

280
00:17:53,660 --> 00:17:56,130
-Really!
-Didn't I tell you?

281
00:17:57,170 --> 00:17:59,830
Okay, on to the next stop!

282
00:17:59,830 --> 00:18:03,770
Umm...I have curfew, so...

283
00:18:03,770 --> 00:18:05,840
-Huh? So soon?
-Huh? So soon?

284
00:18:05,840 --> 00:18:06,840
I'm sorry!

285
00:18:06,840 --> 00:18:09,510
It's dangerous for a girl alone...

286
00:18:09,510 --> 00:18:12,350
Don't worry. I'll see her home.

287
00:18:12,350 --> 00:18:14,350
So long, Koyuki.

288
00:18:14,350 --> 00:18:16,280
Take care.

289
00:18:19,020 --> 00:18:21,520
-It's kinda sad.
-Yeah...

290
00:18:21,520 --> 00:18:24,490
Chiba-kun is training to be
a ramen shop owner, right?

291
00:18:24,490 --> 00:18:27,860
And Taira-kun just joined up with
the popular Indies band as a bassist.

292
00:18:27,860 --> 00:18:30,700
And Ryusuke is missing.

293
00:18:30,700 --> 00:18:33,290
Seems like BECK is no more.

294
00:18:34,540 --> 00:18:35,870
Brrr...cold!

295
00:18:35,870 --> 00:18:39,470
Are you all right?
You sound kinda nasal.

296
00:18:39,470 --> 00:18:41,580
See you around, Koyuki.

297
00:18:41,580 --> 00:18:42,980
Don't catch cold!

298
00:18:54,460 --> 00:18:56,150
Huh? Maho?

299
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:01,860
Saku!

300
00:19:07,840 --> 00:19:09,840
It's soo cold outside!

301
00:19:09,840 --> 00:19:11,710
The weather forecast
calls for snow tomorrow.

302
00:19:11,710 --> 00:19:13,670
Oh yeah?

303
00:19:13,670 --> 00:19:16,680
-Let's eat.
-Yeah.

304
00:19:16,680 --> 00:19:19,670
Oh! Potato chips! Ew!
Kimchi flavored!?

305
00:19:20,680 --> 00:19:23,680
So tonight, too, you just
walked her home and that's all?

306
00:19:23,680 --> 00:19:26,690
Unfortunately, we've never
even held hands.

307
00:19:26,690 --> 00:19:27,690
Hmm...

308
00:19:27,690 --> 00:19:29,520
How far have you gone with Maho?

309
00:19:29,520 --> 00:19:31,530
Huh? I...

310
00:19:31,530 --> 00:19:33,030
I told you before...

311
00:19:33,030 --> 00:19:36,220
Then there's been no progress
since the day of Grateful Sound?

312
00:19:39,970 --> 00:19:44,070
Hey...let's stop!
This was our first live!

313
00:19:44,070 --> 00:19:47,140
Man, it sounds awful!

314
00:19:47,140 --> 00:19:50,310
Remember, Chiba-kun was under
the wrong impression...

315
00:19:50,310 --> 00:19:52,970
And he got it!

316
00:20:05,490 --> 00:20:07,500
-Oh well...
-Saku...

317
00:20:07,500 --> 00:20:09,160
I'm gonna go.

318
00:20:09,160 --> 00:20:11,330
-I'll walk with you.
-Okay.

319
00:20:11,330 --> 00:20:13,330
-Hey Koyuki...
-Yeah?

320
00:20:13,330 --> 00:20:13,990
Huh?!

321
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:17,330
It's snowing!

322
00:20:25,510 --> 00:20:27,170
It's freezing!

323
00:20:28,020 --> 00:20:29,350
Cold!

324
00:20:29,350 --> 00:20:30,850
Cold!!

325
00:20:30,850 --> 00:20:32,520
Damn, it's cold!

326
00:20:32,520 --> 00:20:34,860
It's so cold!

327
00:20:34,860 --> 00:20:37,120
Cold!

328
00:20:37,120 --> 00:20:39,250
-Cold!
-Cold!

329
00:20:45,130 --> 00:20:47,130
Well good-bye, Koyuki.

330
00:20:47,130 --> 00:20:49,030
Take care, Saku.

331
00:20:51,310 --> 00:20:55,140
I'll find a part-time job and save
enough money to live on my own.

332
00:20:55,140 --> 00:20:58,810
I'll convince my parents
and come back in the spring.

333
00:20:58,810 --> 00:21:02,150
In order to revive BECK
with the original members...

334
00:21:02,150 --> 00:21:05,310
I'll quit school and come back!

335
00:21:06,320 --> 00:21:08,310
Uh-huh.

336
00:21:20,170 --> 00:21:21,170
Take care!

337
00:21:21,170 --> 00:21:22,160
You too, Saku!

338
00:21:31,180 --> 00:21:32,980
That was a great piece.

339
00:21:33,350 --> 00:21:34,180
What's your name?

340
00:21:34,180 --> 00:21:37,410
-Yuji Sakurai -a senior in Group 2.
-You're...

341
00:21:37,690 --> 00:21:39,350
I wanted to give this to you.

342
00:21:39,350 --> 00:21:40,960
It's the Dying Breed's
live concert in Germany.

343
00:21:40,960 --> 00:21:44,630
Did you read the interview
of Eddy Lee in Guitar World?

344
00:21:44,630 --> 00:21:47,530
There are two types
of people in this world.

345
00:21:47,530 --> 00:21:50,200
Clever people and obedient people.

346
00:21:50,200 --> 00:21:55,040
Clever people think that the world moves
because of laws and morals created by man.

347
00:21:55,040 --> 00:21:57,540
They think it's everything.

348
00:21:57,540 --> 00:22:00,540
But I don't bother with any of that.

349
00:22:00,540 --> 00:22:01,840
Isn't Eddy amazing?

350
00:22:02,540 --> 00:22:05,600
So, you're in a band?

351
00:22:16,220 --> 00:22:17,660
Koyuki!

352
00:22:43,550 --> 00:22:48,920
Full moon sways

353
00:22:50,390 --> 00:22:56,390
Gently in the night of one fine day

354
00:22:56,390 --> 00:22:59,100
What a fool

355
00:22:59,100 --> 00:23:02,570
I don't know 'bout tomorrow

356
00:23:02,570 --> 00:23:07,400
What it's like to be

357
00:23:07,400 --> 00:23:09,400
Ah...

358
00:23:10,570 --> 00:23:12,410
I was fool

359
00:23:12,410 --> 00:23:16,580
Couldn't let myself to go

360
00:23:16,580 --> 00:23:21,350
Even though I feel

361
00:23:21,350 --> 00:23:27,260
The end

362
00:23:46,210 --> 00:23:51,740
Full moon sways

363
00:23:53,050 --> 00:24:00,080
Smiling in my arms for all those years

364
00:24:13,500 --> 00:24:15,670
Next week: 'America'

365
00:24:15,670 --> 00:24:17,840
Our journey continues.

366
00:24:17,840 --> 00:24:20,340
Although it's the end
of my ramen shop.
